Nuitka 4.3.1 (MSVC cl 14.3, PyQt6 6.11.0, Qt 6.11.2, Python 3.14.10) on Windows 11, in a throwaway venv (%TEMP%\m10-build)
installed as packaging/README.md says: requirements-build.txt with --require-hashes, then requirements.txt with
--no-build-isolation. On a scratch copy of the tree with a throwaway chatmon/locale/de.po, packaging/build.py's own
nuitka() built the program (all of its own options), given windows()'s --experimental=force-dependencies-pefile and a
console (not the icon, names and versions), with packaging/entry.py replaced by the probe below: Chatmon's own entry
would start the whole app.

